{
  // X-Tension's ship roster. XBTF has its own in games/xbtf; the two executables disagree on
  // most numbers, so neither game borrows the other's.
  //
  // Each entry has two halves. Everything above "// ours" is the original game's own data, read
  // from the ship table compiled into the executable — regenerate it with
  //     dotnet run --project tools/OpenXt.AssetImport -- ships --game xtension --json
  // Speed and acceleration are in the m/s the game displays (raw / 222, calibrated against
  // elite-games.ru's ship database; the X-Tension manual prints the raw numbers as if they were m/s).
  // Ship statistics are facts about the game, not copyrighted assets, so they live here; meshes,
  // textures and the games' text never do. Body and text ids are the table's own pairing.
  //
  // Below "// ours" is hand-authored: the game has no notion of mass, so mass, manoeuvring thrust,
  // turn rates and the collision radius are set per class and race and tuned by feel. Two flight
  // values follow the game: cruiseSpeed = speed, mainThrust = mass x acceleration.
  //
  // Cross-checked against elite-games.ru's X-Tension ship database (shipsm5/m4/m3/ts/tl):
  // speed, speedMax, acceleration, power, cargo, cargoMax and the equipment maxima (lasers,
  // shields, best missile) agree for every ship it lists. The prices (priceS/M/L, the
  // shipyard's S, M and L variants; a TL has one price, stored as priceS) come from that
  // database, since the executable's table has none; ships it lists as capture-only have
  // no price. Hull, rudder tunings and missile count are decoded from fields nothing
  // confirms. Steering is stored as found; how the info screen's turn % derives from it is
  // not established.
  //
  // Left out on purpose: stations, satellites, mines, laser towers, fighter drones, space
  // flies, the Commandship (2901), training drones (2911), a second Paranid Prometheus record
  // (body 705, a plot ship) and other "Unknown Object" props.
  //
  // A mod changes this roster by layering its own data/ships/ships.json; entries merge by id.
